All 8 stage groups render in board order (To Do, Research, Plan, Design, Breakdown, Build, Verify, Done); empty groups collapse rather than render an empty shelf — the list above is the design-page sample. Done rows swap the priority pill for a green Done pill; the Done group head ring renders green filled. Rows carry the trailing 22px assignee avatar chip (initials in meta here). The inline five-facet filter row and its accent-ring toggle are REMOVED (WP-N3, docs G4 precedent) — the five facets (sort, type, stage, priority, assignee) live in the anchored filter sheet (`modals/filter.surf`, Tasks vocabulary), opened from the Filter button; the task count sits in the title row before the actions. The list ⇄ board switch is the `segmented-control` block (compact pill single-select) — it replaces the tab-bar stand-in the coverage matrix flagged.

## Board view

Board mode releases the surface's 880px column: the scrollport is true full-bleed — cards clip at the nav edge (left) and screen edge (right) — with an always-visible styled horizontal scrollbar. Transparent lanes, uppercase muted column heads with counts, 12px cards with colored type tiles + @assignee + priority pill, native drag-drop moves the task's stage (`action=moveTaskStage`). At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the board STACKS VERTICALLY: columns render full-width in board order, the horizontal scrollport is gone (height auto, no lane scrolling), and cards flow down the page.

::diagram[type=kanban title="Board view — all 8 SDLC stages in board order"]
column To Do
  Gather Donovan's account details
  Verify DMARC policy
column Research
  Real-time message display
column Plan
column Design
column Breakdown
column Build
  Android audit remediation — Batch 3
column Verify
column Done
  Android new-tabs alignment
::

### Static board markup (WP-C5 — the shape the live `?view=board` route serves)

Board mode is REAL block markup, not prose: stage columns author as a column-head
toolbar (uppercase head text with the count) followed by that stage's card rows,
all 8 stages in board order — empty stages keep their head so the column skeleton
reads. Never the source-driven kanban block (`source=` boards are a different
lane). The horizontal lane scrollport + colored type tiles from the diagram above
are chrome the renderer does not emit for authored blocks yet (renderer-level gap,
LOGGED for the 0.14.1 round); until then the columns stack vertically — the R-C
small-width treatment at every width. The list ⇄ board segmented-control NAVIGATES
between the views (`?view=board`); selection is server-stamped, never faked.

